{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3978","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3978","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3978\",\"parent_revision\":\"259dcd5c63f7c347ed6b65d8dd5d44c356f7adbf5504c5b0e655ea29877c66f5\",\"root_revision\":\"259dcd5c63f7c347ed6b65d8dd5d44c356f7adbf5504c5b0e655ea29877c66f5\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: needs-grooming\\nadded: 2026-09-27\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nA REST 403 for the primary rate limit ('API rate limit exceeded', RateLimitExceededException, often without a Retry-After header) is classified NON_RETRYABLE by sync_state._classify_github_exception. Sync then goes OFFLINE and MCP responses report retryable: false while the limit is only temporary. Found by Codex on #3968 (PRRT_kwDOQGimCs6mbw5i); the behaviour predates #3968.\\n\\nUser-provided context: classify RateLimitExceededException as retryable before the generic 403 rule, and take the delay from x-ratelimit-reset when Retry-After is absent.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session 2026-09-27: live e2e / GitHub robustness work (#3968, #3969, #3975)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-27\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"aaee1064e5f8829a04e493ccd3ea7e219fe5f08888bc55e000a1579135c1eb6f\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABXUvesw\",\"fields\":{\"followup_to\":\"\",\"close_comment\":\"\",\"plan\":\"\",\"item_type\":\"Bug\",\"priority\":\"P1\",\"topic\":\"\",\"close_reference\":\"\",\"research_first\":\"\",\"files\":\"\",\"language\":\"\",\"stack\":\"\",\"source\":\"Session 2026-09-27: live e2e / GitHub robustness work (#3968, #3969, #3975)\",\"status\":\"in-progress\",\"suggested_location\":\"\",\"groomed\":\"\",\"close_reason\":\"\",\"layer\":\"\",\"added\":\"2026-09-27\"}}"}